2DA V1.0
*
           AT_1       AT_2       AT_3       AT_4       TYPE       SPACE      PALETTE    SIZE
0x6500     CPM1       CPM1       CPM1       CPM1       0          2          0          L
0x6501     CPM2       CPM2       CPM2       CPM2       0          2          0          L
0x6510     CPF1       CPF1       CPF1       CPF1       0          2          0          L
# ethren (M2.11): our character animations (tools/sprite_render writes the rows; the test games merge
# them into the demo's table). The engine uses the row with the largest id not above the CRE's, so each
# body owns a block of 16 ids (variants, outfits) and each species and gender a block of 0x10 bodies:
#   0x6500 human male    0x6510 human female   0x6520 dwarf male      0x6530 dwarf female
#   0x6540 elf male      0x6550 elf female     0x6560 halfling male   0x6570 halfling female
# 0x6500 CPM1 the male peasant, hair and beard baked in; 0x6501 CPM2 the same body bald and beardless,
# for the hair and beard overlays (dcchair.2da); 0x6510 CPF1 the female peasant. TYPE 0 (IE_ANI_CODE_MIRROR),
# SPACE 2, PALETTE 0 (recoloured from the CRE's colours), SIZE L: the overlays' WQL* files.
